{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3635","published":"2026-09-05T15:03:21Z","modified":"2026-09-05T15:16:27.377565929Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-18917","CVE-2026-61477","CVE-2026-63622"],"summary":"libvirt security update","details":"Libvirt is a C toolkit to interact with the virtualization capabilities of recent versions of Linux (and other OSes). The main package includes the libvirtd server exporting the virtualization support.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in libvirt. An unprivileged local user could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability in the NodeGetFreePages RPC handler. This flaw allows crafted values to bypass a size check, leading to an undersized memory buffer. Subsequently, real NUMA node data can overwrite this buffer. This heap buffer overflow can corrupt the root libvirt daemon&apos;s memory, potentially leading to a denial of service or local privilege escalation.(CVE-2026-18917)\n\nAn injection vulnerability was found in libvirt&apos;s virtual network driver. The network XML parser does not strip newline characters from DNS TXT record value attributes and SRV record domain/target attributes. These values are written verbatim into the dnsmasq configuration file generated by the network driver, allowing a user with permission to define virtual networks to inject arbitrary dnsmasq configuration directives such as dhcp-script, leading to arbitrary command execution as root.(CVE-2026-61477)\n\nA flaw was found in libvirt. A local attacker, specifically a process running as the confined `swtpm` user, could exploit a symlink-following vulnerability in the `virFileChownFiles()` function. By planting a symbolic link within the `swtpm` state directory, the attacker could trick the root-level libvirt daemon into changing the ownership of an arbitrary file to the `swtpm` user. This allows for privilege escalation from the `swtpm` sandbox to root-level file ownership control.(CVE-2026-63622)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libvirt","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/libvirt&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libvirt-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-client-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-common-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-config-network-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-config-nwfilter-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-interface-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-network-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-nodedev-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-nwfilter-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-qemu-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-secret-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-core-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-disk-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-gluster-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-iscsi-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-iscsi-direct-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-logical-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-mpath-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-rbd-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-scsi-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-kvm-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-lock-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-log-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-plugin-lockd-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-plugin-sanlock-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-proxy-9.10.0-37.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-qemu-9.1